[thin] Left as drawn by Derek on its print history: the rear corners, where the rounded skin, the cylindrical neck opening and the rear lower trim meet, leave a knife edge the lint reads 0.62/0.63 mm across. The cover has been printed and used many times, the successful fan-off cover among them (../../../faucet/sculpted/prints/2026-10-17-localized-cooling-display-clearance-mark2/surface-review.json), and that print and verification history is what keeps it as drawn. Derek, 2026-10-22: "I'd rather leave the faucet display cover alone, simply because it has been printed and used so much that I am feeling confident about it. Its the print and verification history there that excludes it."
alternatives: Reconcile the rounded skin, cylindrical neck opening and rear lower trim in a dedicated corner revision, then read the complete opening and display-loading envelope. A uniform rear trim does not address their intersection; a blanket wall-thickness increase changes the retained flexure.
